[docs] Document the controls library and sample workflow (complete)
Files: game-developer-guide.md; crates/voxel-sample/README.md; proposals/controls-library.md; evidence/clause-to-test.md
Do: Explain the control-state ownership rule, explicit pixel/viewport and logical/Tau delta units, fixed-focus parabolic time reprojection and its default 350/1000 sweet spot, the automatic/manual/resume lifecycle, the two time axes, viewport layout scaling, the screen layout, and how a game keeps controls and view state outside authoritative GameState.
Accept: A developer can implement the same control path from the guide, distinguish logical time from Tau and absolute values from deltas, identify the generic library versus voxel-specific adaptation, and understand that slider geometry scaling and time reprojection are separate.
-> integration-evidence
